Z||000006||fiero56||08-10-2001||09:41 PM||||We had to do the same thing. I usually just skimmed a few pages, read the last couple of chapters, and wrote essays detailing what I read, and my imagination filled in the gaps. Worked pretty well. 'Course I always tried to read 12 books in the last 3 days of break.<P>Books I have enjoyed either by force or by choice are: anything by Michael Crichton(andromeda strain, airframe is excellent, sphere, etc), catcher in the rye was very good, Time of Terror is very good. There are others, but these are all I can come up with at the moment.||||reg||1
