Z||000008||Black88GT||08-11-2001||12:12 AM||||LOL Phil, I was thinking the same thing.<P>At any rate, I always thought summer reading was B.S. too.  I cheated (omg people do that) and purchased reports on the internet.  I paid around $20 for a 1 year membership to a site and I got 4 reports off it, all were "A" papers.  Not to mention throughout the year I used it for essays too.  Best $20 I ever spent.||||reg||12
Z||000009||Mach10||08-11-2001||03:45 AM||||Hmm. For ones that will really make eyebrows rise, assuming you're allowed to pick your own:<BR>Heat of the Night  (if it isn't banned  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> I can't remember the author right now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )<BR>Brave New World-Aldous(sp?) Huxley (AWESOME book about genetic manipulation and drug culture)<BR>Starship Troopers-Robert A. Heinlein (great book, action-packed, but don't do the report on the movie. It's too different)<BR>Friday-Robert A. Heinlein (great chance for some serious controversey. Need an explanation? Look up the word "Doxy")<BR>Rule of the Bone (not sure the author. It's about a 15-year old runaway druggie. I read it when younger and was able to relate to a lot of it.)<P>That's the 5 I'd recommend. You can get some pretty deep quotes. They should be good for an "A." It's too bad you don't like reading. There's some kick-ass books out there.||||reg||6
Z||000010||artherd||08-11-2001||04:00 AM||||Man, I can go through a novel (a good one... not a crappy one that lots of big shirts tell each other is a 'classic'. THE EMPEROR IS NEKKID! ;) uh, that is to say, I can go through a good novel in a nite or two.<P>I usually am reading 3 or 4 novels at any one time (more than 4 I start to get mixed up, which can actually be fun, so occationally I'll go crazy and start 6 or so :)<P>I absolutely love to read, I only wish I had the talent for writing...  I've got a few ideas though, and 'novel' is on my life's list of stuff to do before I die, so hey. Who knows what the future may bring!<P>PS: Hitchiker's guide to the galexy trilogy &lt;muffled laughter&gt; :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
