Z||000015||FieroHeather||08-11-2001||08:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B><FONT SIZE="1">[b]Side thought:</B></FONT><P>When someone is making you do something, it's never the same as just doing it for yourself.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You are <B>so</B> right btoth!  When I do something on my own initiative, it feels really good.  When someone comes behind me to tell me to do something that I have already planned to do/or are already doing, it discourages me, and I seem to begrudge them more for telling me to do the thing that *I* wanted to do in the first place.<P>Ive been working 40 to 60 hours a week for almost 3 months now.  I only get TWO days off in August--tomorrow being one of them.  I am very excited about having some time off, but READING is one of the last things that I want to do.  It seems that there is a LOT more on my priority list to get done than I'd like there to be.<P>Anyone in the same boat?||||reg||1
